# ============================================================================
#  crDroid 13.0 / itel RS4 (S666LN) build recipe — public-repo exclusions.
#  Everything proprietary, huge, secret, or personal stays LOCAL. The public
#  repo is the RECIPE: local_manifests/, apply-overlays.sh, README, docs.
# ============================================================================

# --- Proprietary stock firmware (5.8 GB, Transsion/itel) — not redistributable ---
itel-RS4-S666LN-28.zip
*.stockfw.zip
COS*.zip

# --- Proprietary MediaTek blobs harvested from stock firmware — not redistributable ---
# 32-bit Mali GPU stack (fallback; apply-overlays documents how to regenerate).
blobs32/
# Patched camera-HAL libs enabling RAW/DNG (from the Itel_RS4_RAW_v2 module).
blobs-camera-raw/
Itel_RS4_RAW_v2.zip
# Stock identity extraction workspace / harvested build.props.
stock-28-extract/
stock-props/

# --- Riza kernel prebuilt — published separately in github.com/riza220201/itel-rs4-kernel ---
# The recipe references it; the raw Image.gz is not vendored here.
kernel-stage/

# --- Private signing keys — NEVER commit (sign platform-privileged code) ---
keys-priv/
*.pk8
*.x509.pem

# --- Proprietary fenrir-signed LK — obtain from the device community ---
s666ln-fenrir-signed.bin

# --- Personal lab journal — kept local, not part of the public recipe ---
JOURNAL.md
TELEGRAM-POST*.md
# RESUME*.md, not just RESUME-THIS.md (the AOSPA filename): this project's copy is
# RESUME.md and slipped past the old pattern. It carries the device serial, the
# build-VM ssh alias and key filename — local-only, like the journal.
RESUME*.md

# --- Built ROM zips (multi-GB) — released via Telegram/Drive, never vendored ---
out-zips/
*.zip

# --- Device-tree backup tarball — KimelaZX/device_itel_S666LN was deleted (404),
#     so this 66 MB tgz is currently the only copy besides the build VM. It gets
#     republished as its own repo with attribution, not committed into the recipe.
device-tree-backup/

# --- Abandoned raw-super flashable — kept locally, NOT published ---
# Complete and working, but dropped by operator decision: writing super directly
# bypasses update_engine, so nothing cleans up Virtual A/B snapshot state and a
# raw dd is one-shot with no rollback. Shipping it inside the public recipe would
# read as an install path, which it is not. The install path is the signed OTA zip.
flashable/
build-flashable.sh
build-super.sh

# --- Screenshots / scratch notes ---
*.png
*.jpg
opus 5 method of making infinix both strong and pass e-kyc.txt

# --- Build outputs / logs / cruft ---
out/
*.log
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store

# Local post-flash verification helper. Kept OUT of the public recipe on purpose:
# it is a working tool tied to whatever build is being tested, not an install
# step, and RESUME.md points at it. (The predecessor lived in a session
# scratchpad and was lost when the session ended -- hence a stable path here.)
release-gate.sh

# Raw memory / partition dumps pulled off the device during debugging. These are
# verbatim RAM contents and can carry anything that was resident at the time —
# never publish them. (charger-ramoops was a 917K ramoops dump taken while
# chasing the offline-charging bug.)
charger-ramoops
*-ramoops
*.ramoops
ramoops*.bin

# Working notes kept local. This repo is the build RECIPE; the narrative of how
# each bug was found belongs with the device-tree project, not here.
BYPASS-CHARGING-PROOF.md
ONDEVICE-TEST-CHECKLIST.md

# Editor/script backups. apply-overlays writes these when it patches itself.
*.bak
*.bak-*
